{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'head -n 115 browser-tests.py && tail -n 14 scene.js'","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"Controller, keyboard, touch, audio, and menu integration checks.\n\nRun with the installed Playwright Python, passing an optional HTML path.\nUses the actual self-contained deliverable over file://; no server required.\n\"\"\"\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sys\n\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\n\n\npassed = 0\nfailed = 0\nerrors = []\n\n\ndef check(name, callback):\n    global passed, failed\n    try:\n        callback()\n        passed += 1\n    except Exception as error:\n        failed += 1\n        print(f\"FAIL {name}: {str(error).splitlines()[0]}\")\n\n\ndef require(condition, message):\n    if not condition:\n        raise AssertionError(message)\n\n\nPAD_STUB = \"\"\"\nwindow.__pad={id:'DualSense scripted standard pad',index:0,connected:true,mapping:'standard',timestamp:0,\n axes:[0,0,0,0],buttons:Array.from({length:18},()=>({pressed:false,touched:false,value:0}))};\nnavigator.getGamepads=()=>[window.__pad,null,null,null];\nwindow.__setPad=(indices=[],axes=[0,0,0,0])=>{\n __pad.buttons.forEach((b,i)=>{b.pressed=indices.includes(i);b.touched=b.pressed;b.value=b.pressed?1:0;});\n __pad.axes=axes;__pad.timestamp=performance.now();\n};\n\"\"\"\n\n\ndef state(page):\n    return page.evaluate(\"__game.getState()\")\n\n\ndef ui(page):\n    return page.evaluate(\"__game.getUI()\")\n\n\ndef goto_title(page):\n    page.evaluate(\"__setPad(); __game.action('title')\")\n    page.wait_for_timeout(120)\n    require(state(page)[\"phase\"] == \"title\", \"return-to-title failed\")\n\n\ndef set_range(page, selector, value):\n    page.locator(selector).evaluate(\n        \"(el,value)=>{el.value=String(value);el.dispatchEvent(new Event('input',{bubbles:true}));}\", value\n    )\n\n\ndef pad(page, buttons=None, axes=None, milliseconds=110):\n    page.evaluate(\"([buttons,axes])=>__setPad(buttons,axes)\", [buttons or [], axes or [0, 0, 0, 0]])\n    page.wait_for_timeout(milliseconds)\n\n\ndef pad_press(page, button):\n    pad(page, [button])\n    pad(page)\n\n\ndef ready(page):\n    page.wait_for_function(\"window.__gameReady===true || !!window.__gameError\", timeout=90000)\n    require(page.evaluate(\"window.__gameReady===true\"), page.evaluate(\"window.__gameError || 'boot failed'\"))\n    page.wait_for_timeout(180)\n\n\ntarget = Path(sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else Path(__file__).with_name(\"game.html\")).resolve()\nwith sync_playwright() as playwright:\n    browser = playwright.chromium.launch(headless=True, args=[\n        \"--enable-unsafe-webgpu\", \"--enable-features=Vulkan\", \"--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader\", \"--no-sandbox\"\n    ])\n    context = browser.new_context(viewport={\"width\": 1600, \"height\": 900}, device_scale_factor=1)\n    context.add_init_script(PAD_STUB)\n    page = context.new_page()\n    page.on(\"pageerror\", lambda error: errors.append(f\"desktop: {error}\"))\n    page.goto(target.as_uri(), wait_until=\"load\")\n    boot_ok = False\n    try:\n        ready(page)\n        boot_ok = True\n        passed += 1\n    except Exception as error:\n        failed += 1\n        print(f\"FAIL standalone file boot: {str(error).splitlines()[0]}\")\n\n    if boot_ok:\n        def engines():\n            require(page.evaluate(\"__game.scene.ready.webgpu === true\"), \"WebGPU backend was not selected\")\n            require(page.evaluate(\"__game.physicsVersion === '0.19.3'\"), \"Rapier version does not match 0.19.3\")\n            require(not page.evaluate(\"__game.net.active\"), \"standalone file incorrectly entered a Hub session\")\n            require(page.evaluate(\"__game.audio.diagnostics().music === .1\"), \"music did not default to 10%\")\n        check(\"requested engines and default music\", engines)\n\n        def title_space():\n            page.locator('#title [data-action=\"start\"]').focus()\n            page.keyboard.press(\"Space\")\n            page.wait_for_timeout(180)\n            require(state(page)[\"phase\"] == \"defense\", \"Space did not activate focused launch button\")\n        check(\"keyboard Space activates title\", title_space)\n\n        def pause_freezes():\n            page.keyboard.press(\"Escape\")\n            page.wait_for_timeout(100)\n    sync('enemies',state.enemies,()=>{const g=saucer(0xf58f79);sphere(g,0xf98077,[0,.72,0],[.13,.2,.1]);return g;},(obj,item)=>{obj.position.set(item.x,item.y,.6);obj.rotation.z=Math.sin(t*4+item.id)*.12;});\n    sync('effects',state.effects,item=>{\n      const g=new THREE.Group();const col=item.kind==='rescue'?0xa6ffd4:item.kind==='hit'?0xff886b:0xffd78c;\n      const r=ring(g,col,[0,0,0],[1,1,1]);r.name='burstRing';\n      for(let j=0;j<9;j++){const a=j/9*Math.PI*2;const s=piece(g,GEO.ico,col,[Math.cos(a),Math.sin(a),0],[.12,.12,.12],false);s.name='spark';s.userData.a=a;}\n      return g;\n    },(obj,item)=>{const f=1-Math.max(0,item.life)/(item.maxLife||.65);obj.position.set(item.x,item.y,2);obj.scale.setScalar(.25+f*(item.kind==='pulse'?9:2));obj.children.forEach(c=>{c.visible=f<.92;if(c.name==='spark')c.scale.setScalar(Math.max(.02,(1-f)*.2));});obj.rotation.z=f*.4;});\n    if(phase==='warp'){mother.position.z=Math.sin((state.phaseTime||0)*2)*.8;mother.scale.setScalar(1+(state.phaseTime||0)*.06);}else mother.position.z=0;\n    renderer.render(scene,camera);frames++;\n  }\n  function resize(){const w=canvas.clientWidth||innerWidth,h=canvas.clientHeight||innerHeight;renderer.setSize(w,h,false);const aspect=w/h;const halfH=Math.max(10.125,18/aspect);camera.left=-halfH*aspect;camera.right=halfH*aspect;camera.top=halfH;camera.bottom=-halfH;camera.updateProjectionMatrix();}\n  resize();addEventListener('resize',resize);\n  return {render,resize,renderer,camera,scene,ready:{webgpu:Boolean(renderer.backend?.isWebGPUBackend),three:THREE.REVISION,animation:'AnimationMixer / AnimationClip',get frames(){return frames;}},dispose(){removeEventListener('resize',resize);renderer.dispose();}};\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='index.template.html';s=open(p).read().replace('body.touch .sceneTag{bottom:15vh}}','body.touch .sceneTag{bottom:15vh}body.touch .stats{position:absolute;top:16px;right:84px}}');open(p,'w').write(s)\np='browser-tests.py';s=open(p).read();needle='        check(\\\"touch runtime has no uncaught errors\\\", lambda: require(not errors, \\\"; \\\".join(errors)))';extra='''        def touch_landscape_title():\n            phone.evaluate(\\\"__game.action('title')\\\")\n            phone.set_viewport_size({\\\"width\\\":844,\\\"height\\\":390})\n            phone.wait_for_timeout(180)\n            layout = phone.evaluate(\\\"\\\"\\\"(()=>{const t=document.querySelector('#title');const brand=t.querySelector('.brandline').getBoundingClientRect();const heading=t.querySelector('h1').getBoundingClientRect();return {clear:heading.top>=brand.bottom,fit:[...t.querySelectorAll('button')].every(b=>{const r=b.getBoundingClientRect();return r.left>=0&&r.right<=innerWidth&&r.bottom<=innerHeight-20})}})()\\\"\\\"\\\")\n            require(layout[\\\"clear\\\"], \\\"landscape heading overlaps brand\\\")\n            require(layout[\\\"fit\\\"], \\\"landscape title actions are clipped\\\")\n        check(\\\"short landscape touch title remains fully usable\\\", touch_landscape_title)\n''';s=s.replace(needle,extra+needle);open(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\nnode build.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='index.template.html';s=open(p).read().replace('body.touch .sceneTag{bottom:15vh}}','body.touch .sceneTag{bottom:15vh}body.touch .stats{position:absolute;top:16px;right:84px}}');open(p,'w').write(s)\np='browser-tests.py';s=open(p).read();needle='        check(\\\"touch runtime has no uncaught errors\\\", lambda: require(not errors, \\\"; \\\".join(errors)))';extra='''        def touch_landscape_title():\n            phone.evaluate(\\\"__game.action('title')\\\")\n            phone.set_viewport_size({\\\"width\\\":844,\\\"height\\\":390})\n            phone.wait_for_timeout(180)\n            layout = phone.evaluate(\\\"\\\"\\\"(()=>{const t=document.querySelector('#title');const brand=t.querySelector('.brandline').getBoundingClientRect();const heading=t.querySelector('h1').getBoundingClientRect();return {clear:heading.top>=brand.bottom,fit:[...t.querySelectorAll('button')].every(b=>{const r=b.getBoundingClientRect();return r.left>=0&&r.right<=innerWidth&&r.bottom<=innerHeight-20})}})()\\\"\\\"\\\")\n            require(layout[\\\"clear\\\"], \\\"landscape heading overlaps brand\\\")\n            require(layout[\\\"fit\\\"], \\\"landscape title actions are clipped\\\")\n        check(\\\"short landscape touch title remains fully usable\\\", touch_landscape_title)\n''';s=s.replace(needle,extra+needle);open(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\nnode build.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"Built The-Great-Space-Escape-Cosmic-Ark-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212558.html\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > qa-log.json <<'EOF'\n[\n {\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Rapier descriptor used a rigid-body instance method\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"critical\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"fixed\\\"},\n {\\\"issue\\\":\\\"String replacement interpreted dollar sequences and corrupted the single-file JavaScript bundle\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"critical\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"fixed\\\"},\n {\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Star points were subpixel and invisible\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"minor\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"fixed\\\"},\n {\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Visual state contract did not reflect delivered creatures, lift progress and directional aiming\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"major\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"fixed\\\"},\n {\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Dock and tractor beam range lacked visual guides\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"major\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"fixed\\\"},\n {\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Attract mode left a shortened defense duration in player balance\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"major\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"fixed\\\"},\n {\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Space could not activate focused menu buttons\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"major\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"fixed\\\"},\n {\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Mouse motion did not exit attract mode\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"minor\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"fixed\\\"},\n {\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Keyboard arrows could change settings sliders by two steps\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"minor\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"fixed\\\"},\n {\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Mouse menu clicks did not update last-input glyph selection\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"minor\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"fixed\\\"},\n {\\\"issue\\\":\\\"The title could appear while waiting for an AI Hub round\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"major\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"fixed\\\"},\n {\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Short landscape touch title clipped actions and overlapped its brand\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"major\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"fixed\\\"},\n {\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Title tableau included duplicate overlapping creatures\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"minor\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"fixed\\\"},\n {\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Ground creatures appeared to hover above the terrain\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"minor\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"fixed\\\"},\n {\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Disconnected pilots could affect sentries or strand their cargo\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"major\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"fixed\\\"},\n {\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Landscape touch status panel obscured the ark cockpit\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"minor\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"fixed\\\"}\n]\nEOF\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('credits.json');d=json.loads(p.read_text())\nd['sourceInformation']['testing']='20 simulation checks including complete solo and four-pilot campaigns; 17 Chromium browser checks with file://, virtual controller, touch and generated audio; 16 network unit checks; 54 AI Hub checks across four scenarios; 17 build/metadata checks. Real controller, iOS hardware and listening feedback: unknown.'\nd['testingFeedback']=[\n'Testing and visual/code review caught 16 actionable issues; all fixed and recorded in qa-log.json.',\n'2 critical issues: a Rapier descriptor API mismatch and literal-string bundle corruption. Both fixed.',\n'The complete automated solo and four-pilot campaigns validated every world, all twelve rescues, and the final victory; the real AI Hub harness validated four network scenarios.',\n'Headless WebGPU screenshots were blank. Renderer-state checks and headed compatibility screenshots provided useful evidence instead.'\n]\nd['engineFeedback']=[\n'Three.js TSL made stepped cel shading and reusable procedural materials straightforward; AnimationMixer animated the creatures and engines.',\n'Used a rigid-body instance method on a Rapier descriptor; installed type definitions gave the correct method. Literal HTML insertion also needed replacement callbacks to preserve dollar signs.',\n'The alternating defense/rescue simulation, controller menu navigation and host-authoritative cooperative world.',\n'Headless WebGPU image capture and multi-iframe SwiftShader device loss. Single-page WebGPU checks passed; some harness frames used the renderer’s WebGL2 fallback.',\n'none',\n'More reliable headless WebGPU screenshots and clearer backend/device-loss diagnostics.'\n]\np.write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nout=dict(d)\nout['aiHub']={\n'name':'The Great Space Escape',\n'tagline':'Small ship. Strange cargo. Last chance.',\n'description':'Defend a tiny ark from four directions, then swoop down to tractor-beam strange creatures to safety. Rescue twelve passengers across three hand-built worlds and hold the line through one final storm, alone or with a crew.',\n'type':'Game','genre':'Shooter','source':'Cosmic Ark (1982)','series':'','players':'1–4',\n'controls':'WASD / left stick: aim or fly; Space / mouse / R2: shoot or beam; Shift / Cross: pulse or boost; Esc / Options: pause; touch: drag left, assisted fire/beam, double-tap right to boost.',\n'tags':['arcade','co-op','sci-fi','retro','2.5d','vehicles']}\nPath('../exit-interview.json').write_text(json.dumps(out,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nPY\ncat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# The Great Space Escape\n\nAn original arcade rescue game inspired by Cosmic Ark (1982). Three worlds, twelve strange passengers, and one final meteor storm. Fixed front orthographic 2.5D, cel shading and ink silhouettes, all procedural geometry and audio.\n\nOpen the HTML file in the parent folder directly in a current WebGPU-capable browser. All game dependencies, including Rapier's WASM, are bundled: no CDN or server is needed for standalone play. Music defaults to 10%. Audio unlocks on the first input.\n\n- WASD / left stick: aim in four directions during defense; fly during rescue.\n- Space / left mouse / R2: fire or hold the tractor beam. Mouse aims in defense; click and drag a destination in rescue.\n- Shift / Cross (Xbox A): shield pulse in defense; boost in rescue.\n- Escape / Options: pause. Developer tools are available from pause, with live balance sliders, defaults, repair and phase advance.\n- A second local pilot uses a second standard gamepad or arrows + Enter + Right Ctrl.\n- Touch: invisible left stick, assisted shooting and tractor beam, right-side aiming, double-tap right to boost.\n\nFly below the dashed range line and hold a beam steady over a creature. Carry two, then return to the dock beneath the ark. Four creatures per world; six shared hull points. Finish all three worlds and survive the final storm. The title runs an AI demonstration after ten idle seconds; any input returns to the title.\n\nStandalone supports one or two local pilots. AI Hub sessions support one to four pilots with a shared authoritative world. The unmodified AI Hub session client is the first script in the document. Four required harness scenarios pass: two players, four with latency/jitter/loss, host departure, and a host with no player.\n\n## Rebuild\n\n\"'`npm ci --ignore-scripts` then `npm run build` (requires Bun). Versions: Three.js 0.180.0, Rapier 0.19.3. The build writes the deliverable into the parent folder and an identical `game.html` for the harness.\n\n## Test\n\nRun `python3 test.py` from this folder. It runs all 124 automated checks sequentially and prints only failures plus one final count. It uses this workstation'\"'s existing Python Playwright environment; browsers are not downloaded. Tests open file:// directly except the AI Hub suite, which creates a temporary HTTP server bound to 127.0.0.1 on an OS-selected port, validates the served game, and terminates its own server by PID.\n\nCoverage: build integrity and credits, Rapier collision and complete campaign simulation, disconnected pilots, network protocol unit tests, actual keyboard and virtual standard controller, touch portrait/landscape, generated and live audio levels, ten-second attract behavior, and all required AI Hub scenarios. \"'`qa-log.json` records the 16 issues fixed during development.\n\nVisual references: `ui-tv-title.png`, `ui-tv-rescue.png`, and phone images in this folder. Headless WebGPU screenshots may be blank, so visuals were reviewed through a headed compatibility renderer. Standalone WebGPU initialization is checked directly. Software WebGPU across multiple harness iframes sometimes loses a device and falls back to WebGL2; protocol/game state checks passed. Physical controller, actual iPhone and subjective audio listening remain unknown.\n\nSource information, testing feedback, engine feedback and prompt feedback are in the game'\"'s About / Credits screen and in the parent folder's \"'`exit-interview.json`. Usage is added on import.\nEOF\nnode build.mjs'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
